{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And I will establish My covenant with you.</b> This covenant is what He stipulates with him now: that they will perish and he will endure, and all of them will be wiped out in the Flood while he is saved; or it may allude to the covenant of the rainbow." "<b>And.</b> The Ramban, of blessed memory, wrote: And according to the way of truth, the covenant is from the world of היא, and the word is derived from בראשית ברא אלהים — and so בריתי is like ברייתי, and the word is as though construct-bound, for it is bound to the worlds that were before us, and He commanded that it arise and be with the righteous; and likewise ״ואני הנני מקים את בריתי אתכם״ (Malachi 2:5), ״בריתי היתה אתו״ — and the discerning will understand, end of quote. And the meaning of his explanation that the covenant is emanated from the world — it is mercy, and bound to the worlds, for it is the governance of the worlds; it will arise and be with the righteous, the foundation of the world, and through it they receive influx and bestow below — this is what is meant by אתכם."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:10:47.689379552Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}